// The Old Orchard (Orchard_2; bible 4.4, 7.1 step 5, 8.4). The only place in Halden with fallen leaves.
// Isolde's cache: her torn pages, the Stillness measured, and five names (reveal 5.1). The pages speak in her
// voice: plain, questions instead of answers. The Orchard Keeper knew Corvin (8.4 [F 5.4]); the gravestone.

title: Orchard_Isolde_Cache
---
<<if has_flag("isolde.cache")>>
    Pages: Five who could hold a place without me. Go and find out if I was right.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pages: Journeyman. If you are reading this, you came the long way. Good. Look at the leaves.
Pages: They fall here. Nowhere else in Halden does anything fall. Why not? #plant:5.1
Pages: The market has sold the same eleven stalls of fruit for eleven years. I counted.
Pages: The king is nine. He has been nine since I was your age.
Pages: Anchoring stops the fade. It stops everything else too. The Guild knows. Voss knows.
Pages: So what do we do instead? I don't know. I know five who might.
Pages: Sable, who crosses. Runa, Kettil's girl, who walks. Teodor Ashe, who lets go.
Pages: Idrenne, who never needed any of it. And Pell, if Pell will.
Pages: Don't anchor what I've drawn. Come find why. You're nearly there.
-> She knew I'd come here.
    <<voice surveyor halden>>
-> Then I'll find them. All five.
    <<voice warden halden>>
-> ...
    <<voice drift halden>>
<<flag isolde.cache 1>>
<<flag halden.orchard.cache_read 1>>
===

title: Orchard_Keeper
---
<<if has_flag("halden.orchard.keeper_met")>>
    Keeper: Still raking. Nobody else remembers they fall. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Keeper: You're Isolde's. #plant:5.4
Keeper: She stood where you're standing. Asked about the leaves.
-> You're the only one who rakes them.
    Keeper: Someone has to. Nobody else remembers they fall.
    <<voice surveyor halden>>
-> Where did she go after here?
    Keeper: Down. Same as everyone who asks the right question.
    <<voice warden halden>>
-> ...
    Keeper: That's what she said too.
    <<voice drift halden>>
Keeper: I planted these trees for an owl who kept the Atlas. He liked the leaves. He liked them falling.
<<flag halden.orchard.keeper_met 1>>
===

title: Orchard_Gravestone
---
Inscription: Halloway. A compass rose, and an owl's eye in it.
Inscription: A second name beneath, worn off by rain. Four letters. The first is an I. #plant:5.4
===
